{"title":"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For how many positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/8/238e9dc9796c95dfd48409371c1d239cc91df76b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{10}(x-40) + \\log_{10}(60-x) &lt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"260\" height=\"18\" />&#160;?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/b/04bd0a96dc997a112211865374afdbdff5c9969e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }10\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }18\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }19\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }20\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }\\text{infinitely many}\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"489\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The domain of the LHS implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/1/e61ac4e06141f931a998331029b57ad65f67c533.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[40&lt;x&lt;60\\]\" width=\"94\" height=\"13\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/1/ca113d86123849e85937b4b9bdd4a61fccae0857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"49\" height=\"20\" /> is defined only when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/2/4c28242522f23e896074dc89612847f8317911d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/f/57f1406b65f9f2e6a365b7356da731780b42cceb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\]\" />\nBegin from the left-hand side\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/4/6749fe9dcc8059ce47ccd96766d2b0d9d1f0eb3a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{10}[(x-40)(60-x)]&lt;2\\]\" width=\"210\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/8/dc8b0d61948c16d06b5abed7664d06898e0969c2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x-40)(60-x)&lt;100\\]\" width=\"179\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/b/8cb07d38ab8be9ccbb57dd02425ab79f4a9da74d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-x^2+100x-2500&lt;0\\]\" width=\"181\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/7/dc75fe198e27a34d5b4d4876eed002ce2eb24c26.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x-50)^2&gt;0\\]\" width=\"103\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39c9aefab22bafbe506412f1eeed25a27f7cf9d5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x \\not = 50\\]\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />\nHence, we have integers from 41 to 49 and 51 to 59. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/2/402b4180ea2e008bf92d91d2f46ad61f12d9bb57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} 18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"58\" height=\"28\" /> integers.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This solution is similar to the first solution, but perhaps more clear. \n</p><p>By the properties of logarithms, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/e/41e68acd7bb1941802ca28dfced29f70e7412d14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{10}(x-40)+\\log_{10}(60-x)=\\log_{10}((x-40)(60-x))\\implies\\log_{10}((x-40)(60-x)).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"671\" height=\"20\" /> Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/4/2046f06a86cadce757cb86c9bf6475ef903aa1d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-40)(60-x)&lt;100.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"188\" height=\"20\" /> We can see that this function is concave down (that is, it looks like an upside-down U shape); that is, it has a maximum value. This maximum value is attained at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/0/1f01823e8695b03be2e57d98a777a521d5069ebc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=50$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />, in which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/7/ed78e8c61d6ff550dfe66aa80e7325669fbcb5cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-40)(60-x)=100.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"188\" height=\"20\" /> This is the one point on the function that does not satisfy the given condition. \n</p><p>We also know that, as noted in solution 1, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must be greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, since otherwise, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/e/9beb3154aa95b0c3eb16797be3d5ff39442bfe62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{10}(x-40)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/2/592822b21be9f5418b9bc4d291140087c13fb7c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{10}(60-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" /> would be undefined. Thus, the possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> are the positive integers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3ba6cdde56f366d628a7a35826f98523dbe58bd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$41$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/c/1bcff350da577673126627a9b9fa6869032de351.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$59,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> inclusive, excluding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/3/f6396a14d58628924f3cc5e52c29ae4aa8b0e7b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50.$\" width=\"21\" height=\"12\" /> Thus, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff9bd24dce12d55fb85245b62b30ee5b50c5714.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19-1=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> total integers. \n</p><p>~ Technodoggo\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/RdIIEhsbZKw?t=1088\">https://youtu.be/RdIIEhsbZKw?t=1088</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B\">2014 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017025357\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.042 seconds\nReal time usage: 1.421 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 235/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4871/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.096      1 -total\n 61.06%    7.997      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 37.15%    4.865      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:12424:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017025357 and revision id 262667. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}